id=a52sxq_camera_stock_libs
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: camera ultra wide / selfie shape correction and scene detector libraries
author=kusti420
description=Camera audit 2026-11-14 on the test phone. (1) Ultra wide shape correction never ran: the S26U libPortraitDistortionCorrection.arcsoft.so ships its OpenCL kernels as a binary built for the S26U GPU, which the A52s Adreno 642L driver rejects (PDC_CL "clCreateProgramWithBinary error , -30", "ARC_PDC_PreInit ERROR res = 3"), so libUltraWideDistortionCorrection logged "Correction Failed. Just Copy Input to Output" and every 0.5x photo was saved uncorrected while flagged as corrected. The stock A52s set (UWDC 1.4.7 + PDC 1.1.125231001.360 + Cali, same JNI as the One UI 9 camera's UWDistortionCorrectionEngine) bind-mounted on 9.3.117: ARC_PDC_Init/Process result 0. The S26U libWideDistortionCorrection (needs the newer PDC exports) stays: CAMERA_CONFIG_WIDE_DISTORTION_CORRECTION field 7 is 0 on the A52s, so the camera never uses it. (2) The A52s vendor floating_feature lists selfie_correction.samsung.v1 in CAMERA_CONFIG_VENDOR_LIB_INFO, so the camera's SecSelfieCorrectionNode takes the legacy path (SelfieCorrectionEngine, static System.loadLibrary("FacialBasedSelfieCorrection.camera.samsung")), but the S26U ships no such library. Add the A52s stock one (imports only libOpenCv/libBeauty_v4.camera.samsung + libc/libm/libdl/liblog/libjnigraphics/libc++, all resolved on the ROM) and its public.libraries entry like stock. (3) libSceneDetector_v1.camera.samsung.so: stock A52s ships it in /system/lib64 and lists it as a public camera library; the app's libSceneDetectorJNI (VZClassifier, SribSceneDetectionNode) dlopens it, the S26U has none and only /vendor has a copy apps may not load. Scene optimizer itself runs in the HAL (SceneDetectorPlugin, vendor lib), so this only restores the app-side detector stock has.
